  steps: [
    { math: '1 · Agent, environment, reward', note: 'An agent acts; the environment responds with a new state and a reward number. The goal: a policy (which action in which situation) maximising total future reward. No labels — just scores.' },
    { math: '2 · The credit assignment problem', note: 'A lost chess game had 80 moves — which ones caused the loss? Delayed rewards make blame attribution hard; algorithms discount and propagate reward backwards through time.' },
